      "problem": "${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\operatorname{log}⁡(2-7x)=$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{log}⁡(2-7x).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14250624/assets/b4fcf2946431788963444f22bcd51b2a617b53dfc4bbfdd0d8b90bd9fd9304d2.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the function increases without bound as $x$ decreases. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\operatorname{log}⁡(2-7x)=\\infty \n$$",
